  "conclusion": "Arbitrary unseen bases do not support zero-shot transfer without a relation signal: raw shared memory and explicit view lookup both fail, while exact basis knowledge is nearly perfect. Once a few paired calibration contexts relate the new basis to a learned reference, ordinary linear alignment solves most of the problem; performance rises sharply around and above the rank-4 shared correction subspace. The next unresolved question is whether correspondence/alignment can be recovered without explicit paired context labels."
